Ducks hold on for dear life at the end of the period. Lukáš Dostál should probably thank Drew Helleson on the way back to the locker room.

Flames have doubled the Ducks in shots (14-7), but the Ducks have doubled the Flames on the scoresheet, 2-1, after 1.

@SportingTrib | #FlyTogether

Cutter Gauthier (upper-body, day-to-day) participated in drills to open practice today, but left the ice before line rushes and team drills.

Not known if that was planned or not, yet. Again, more info tomorrow at Ducks morning skate.

@SportingTrib | #FlyTogether

Ducks back in Orange County after their 2-0 Canadian weekender.

Cutter Gauthier (upper-body) on the ice in his normal practice sweater, as is Drew Helleson (lower-body). However, no Ryan Poehling (lower-body).

@SportingTrib | #FlyTogether

And the Ducks' shutout search will last yet another game, as Kyle Connor slips behind the Ducks defense to put one up top. Jets' first shot of the period.

Anaheim has now gone 167 games without a shutout. Its last clean sheet came in the 2024-25 season opener.

@SportingTrib | #FlyTogether

Don't let this Ducks fourth line get out and running!

Washe with an excellent strip back in the D zone, and its off to the races. Caulfield with a great pass to get Malott going, who feeds Washe to double the Ducks' lead.

